  "note": "The Hebrew verb and the crop pest share a clear association with eating a harvest away. The insect names in Ugaritic and Ethiopic have final n where Hebrew has l. Kogan proposes a relationship, but the insects named differ across the languages. The Hebrew passages do not specify a species or a growth stage."
